# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# This file is a cost, not a formality: every `make cloud-build-push` uploads this tree seven times,
# once per image. Excluding the prose corpora takes the upload from ~4 MB to well under one.
#
# The two `!` re-includes below are load-bearing. `deploy/docker/Dockerfile` COPYs `docs/glossary.md`
# (line 92) and `local-dev/okf_frontmatter.py` (line 122) into the agent images, so a blanket
# `docs/` or `local-dev/` exclusion does not make the build smaller -- it makes it fail, at the COPY,
# with a message about a missing file rather than a missing ignore rule. The `dir/*` + `!dir/file`
# shape is deliberate: gitignore semantics cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so `docs/` followed by `!docs/glossary.md` would silently not work.
#
# Verify any change here with:  gcloud meta list-files-for-upload

# Version control
.git
.github

# IDEs and AI agent logs/scratch files
.idea/
.vscode/
.gemini/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build and package caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
k8s-operator/bin/
# Gitignored, but .gitignore is not consulted once this file exists -- so without this line the
# 125 KB coverage profile rides along in all seven uploads.
k8s-operator/cover.out

# Local configuration files (except tracked default .env)
.env
.env.*
!agents/shared/defaults/.env

# Prose and harness corpora. None of this is in any image; docs/ alone is 2.2 MB and the build
# ledger under docs/build/ is most of it.
docs/*
!docs/glossary.md
.claude/
local-dev/*
!local-dev/okf_frontmatter.py
